      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $P$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $P$ has $2$ pivots in the $1$st and $2$nd columns:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column.",
